        "original_id": "c5ed6cbb-cc02-5436-ae2e-7e3a7cd083d0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Trembling Before G-d, Zeitgeist film series, A Jihad for Love\n- People: Sandi Simcha DuBowski, Parvez Sharma\n- Topics: LGBT people and religion, Orthodox Judaism, conspiracy theories, social and economic change\n\nFacts:\n- Trembling Before G-d is a 2001 American documentary film about gay and lesbian Orthodox Jews trying to reconcile their sexuality with their faith.\n- Sandi Simcha DuBowski is an American director and producer known for work about the intersection of LGBT people and religion.\n- Sandi Simcha DuBowski directed the 2001 documentary Trembling Before G-d.\n- Zeitgeist is a series of three documentary films released between 2007 and 2011.\n- The Zeitgeist film series presents conspiracy theories and proposals for broad social and economic changes.\n- Sandi Simcha DuBowski produced Parvez Sharma's 2007 documentary A Jihad for Love, which was formerly known as In the Name of Allah.",
